2026-10-22 16:35:20 GMT Daylight Time | CRITICAL | NeuroSan:_log:815 - NeuroSan - Arguments: ('agent_network_designer.StreamingChat', "'# Build Social Pulse 360 — Automated Brand Monitoring Pipeline\n\nAct as an expert AI agent architect. Build a working multi-agent application called **Social Pulse 360** using the available NeuroSan framework and its supported agent-network configuration format.\n\n## Objective\n\nCreate a brand-monitoring pipeline that processes social media posts, detects spam, protects personal information, analyses sentiment, and generates appropriate response drafts for a brand's social media team.\n\n## Create these three agents\n\n### 1. DataIngesterAgent\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n* Accept social media posts containing an ID, handle, display name, and text.\n* Validate the input and identify missing or invalid fields.\n* Detect duplicate posts.\n* Identify likely spam, scams, suspicious links, and promotional bot messages.\n* Redact personal information where identifiable.\n* Preserve the original post ID for traceability.\n* Pass cleaned post data and spam flags to SentimentAnalystAgent.\n* Do not discard potentially important customer complaints simply because they contain negative language.\n\n### 2. SentimentAnalystAgent\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n* Analyse the cleaned post text.\n* Classify sentiment as Positive, Neutral, or Negative.\n* Identify the primary topic, such as Product Issue, Technical Support, Billing, Feature Request, Product Feedback, or Spam.\n* Assign a priority of Low, Medium, High, or Critical.\n* Explain the reason for the classification.\n* Flag complaints involving outages, repeated unresolved issues, billing problems, or significant customer dissatisfaction for human review.\n* Treat spam flagged by DataIngesterAgent separately from genuine customer feedback.\n\n### 3. ResponseStrategistAgent\n\nResponsibilities:\n\n* Generate a professional, empathetic, brand-safe response draft for genuine customer posts.\n* For positive posts, draft a thank-you message.\n* For neutral questions, draft a helpful response without inventing product capabilities or policies.\n* For negative posts, acknowledge the problem, apologise where appropriate, and suggest a sensible next step.\n* For spam, recommend filtering or moderation rather than drafting a customer-service reply.\n* Recommend human escalation for high-priority complaints.\n* Never claim that an issue has been fixed unless the input confirms it.\n* Never publish or send responses automatically. All responses must remain drafts for human approval.\n\n## Workflow\n\nConfigure the agents to run in this order:\n\nDataIngesterAgent \u2192 SentimentAnalystAgent \u2192 ResponseStrategistAgent\n\nEnsure that each agent receives the previous agent's output and that the original post ID remains associated with the result.\n\n## Output\n\nFor each post, produce structured output containing:\n\n* post_id\n* handle\n* cleaned_text\n* is_spam\n* sentiment\n* topic\n* priority\n* classification_reason\n* response_draft\n* requires_human_review\n* escalation_reason\n\nUse the structured output formats and tool-calling conventions supported by the installed NeuroSan version.\n\n## Implementation requirements\n\n1. Use the actual NeuroSan agent-network schema supported by this installation.\n2. Reuse available framework capabilities instead of inventing unsupported configuration fields.\n3. Create three separate agents and connect them into a functioning workflow.\n4. Make the network callable from the NeuroSan frontend.\n5. If the framework supports file-reading tools, allow the workflow to process a CSV containing social media posts.\n6. If direct CSV processing is not supported through the frontend, explain the smallest additional step needed to process a local CSV file.\n7. Do not invent tool names, APIs, or framework features.\n8. Save or generate the network configuration in the appropriate location if the interface supports it.\n9. Validate the configuration and report any errors.\n10. Provide concise instructions for testing the complete pipeline with sample posts.\n\nPrioritise a working prototype over unnecessary complexity. Do not integrate live social media APIs.\n'")
